      "short": "No real solution.",
      "worked": "$x\\ne-1,4$. Multiply by $(x+1)(x-4)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}(x-1)(x-4)+2x(x+1)&=(x+1)(x-4)\\\\3x^2-3x+4&=x^2-3x-4\\\\2x^2+8&=0\\\\x^2&=-4.\\end{align*}$$\nA real square cannot be negative, so there is no real solution.",
